# Clerk Authentication & Data Isolation

All authentication is handled by [Clerk](https://clerk.com). Do not roll a custom auth system, session store, or user table.

- Server: `await auth()` from `@clerk/nextjs/server` (must `await`)
- Client: `useAuth()`, `useUser()`, `<Show>` from `@clerk/nextjs`
- Middleware: [proxy.ts](mdc:proxy.ts) (`clerkMiddleware`)
- Provider: `ClerkProvider` in [app/layout.tsx](mdc:app/layout.tsx)
- Schema: `decks.userId` stores the Clerk user ID ([db/schema.ts](mdc:db/schema.ts))

## Data isolation (required)

Users may **only** access data they own. Never return, update, or delete another user's decks or cards. Never trust a `userId` from the client — always take it from `auth()`.

1. Require a signed-in user before any data access
2. Scope every deck query with `eq(decks.userId, userId)`
3. Scope card access through the parent deck's ownership (cards have no `userId`)
4. On insert, set `userId` from `auth()`, never from the request body

```typescript
import { auth } from "@clerk/nextjs/server";
import { eq, and } from "drizzle-orm";
import { db } from "@/db";
import { decks, cards } from "@/db/schema";

const { isAuthenticated, userId } = await auth();
if (!isAuthenticated) throw new Error("Unauthorized");

// ✅ decks: always filter by Clerk userId
const userDecks = await db.select().from(decks).where(eq(decks.userId, userId));

await db.insert(decks).values({ userId, name, description });

await db
  .update(decks)
  .set({ name })
  .where(and(eq(decks.id, deckId), eq(decks.userId, userId)));

// ✅ cards: join/filter through the owning deck
const deckCards = await db
  .select({ card: cards })
  .from(cards)
  .innerJoin(decks, eq(cards.deckId, decks.id))
  .where(and(eq(decks.id, deckId), eq(decks.userId, userId)));
```

```typescript
// ❌ never fetch by id alone — leaks other users' data
const deck = await db.select().from(decks).where(eq(decks.id, deckId));
const deckCards = await db.select().from(cards).where(eq(cards.deckId, deckId));

// ❌ never use a client-supplied userId
await db.insert(decks).values({ userId: body.userId, name });
```

Apply this in Server Components, Route Handlers, and Server Actions. Auth in the UI is not enough.
